<title>USA: Wilmington, Del., sees $1.5 mln budget surplus.</title>
<headline>Wilmington, Del., sees $1.5 mln budget surplus.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>City of Wilmington said it would end the 1997 fiscal year with a $1.5 million budget surplus.</p>
<p>Officials released the figure during Tuesday's first budget hearing.</p>
<p>But finance committee members said Wilmington's budget is still going to depend on Mayor Jim Sills' proposed wage tax increase. That tax hike would give the city an additional $6.5 million next year.</p>
